<p></p>
<p><br></p>
<p>The Dimensional Model (EDM) will consist of several entity types and sub=
-types. These are documented below, along with naming standards and standar=
d attributes.</p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-NamingConvention">Naming Conv=
ention</h1>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Entity Type</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Naming Convention (Prefix)</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Fact</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FCT_</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Dimension</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DIM_</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Bridge</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">BRG_</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p>The names of the entities should be descriptive after the prefix, and fo=
llow <span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">the abbreviations list under A1 Standar=
d Abbreviations and Acronyms List<span>&nbsp;</span></span><a href=3D"https=
://confluence.group.net/display/GIBP/LV+Data+Naming+Standards" rel=3D"nofol=
low">here in the LV Data Naming Standards</a></p>
<p>For example:<br><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img cl=
ass=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" src=3D"11616c2224c094=
5894df47ed7f2d51250b9c4a58580ded22154863118ec2d620" data-image-src=3D"/down=
load/attachments/154629394/image2022-9-28_12-41-9.png?version=3D1&amp;modif=
icationDate=3D1664365269000&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160793025" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1"=
 data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alia=
s=3D"image2022-9-28_12-41-9.png" data-base-url=3D"https://confluence.group.=
net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-c=
ontainer-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"27" tab=
index=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468" height=3D"15"></span></p>
<p>In this example, Underwriting has been abbreviated to UNDWG.</p>
<p>Fact table names are likely to be the most arduous, as they should attem=
pt to describe the granularity of the table in the name.&nbsp; It's likely =
that end users won't necessarily see these, as we will resolve a lot of joi=
ns in presentation views for use in their own Gold layer access databases.<=
/p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-StandardRequirements">Standar=
d Requirements</h1>
<p>Each entity will require the PostSQL tab to be populated and the "Genera=
te" option ticked.</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<p>USING DELTA<br>
  LOCATION '/mnt/DataLake/DeltaLake/curated_idw/dim_scheme';</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tablename should be in lower case.</p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Keys">Keys</h1>
<p>Traditionally, surrogate keys in a dimensional model are meaningless inc=
remental numbers.&nbsp; This fulfills a purpose, whereby these keys should =
not be used for anything other than joining the data, but it does come with=
 a performance impact on loading, especially fact tables.&nbsp; Therefore I=
 have come up with a new method using hash keys.</p>
<p>Using HASH keys allows us to generate the same key across all entities a=
t the same time, allowing parallel loading, and although this then gives th=
e keys some meaning, they are still meaningless to consumers of the data.</=
p>
<p>The key will be designed at the point of modelling and behind the scenes=
 really shows the granularity of the dimension; it could be made up of mult=
iple columns and these should be shown in ER Studio as the _UK1 of the enti=
ty for Reference Driven Dimensions (see below).&nbsp; The _PK will be the H=
ASH value itself.</p>
<p>E.G.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"116" src=3D"58cf5b3ec678391a30eaf460f8106e6dc9b02206588f7bc77e1269d342=
6f287b" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-10-5_9-=
42-50.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664959370000&amp;api=3Dv2" da=
ta-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160796814" dat=
a-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" da=
ta-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-10-5_9-42-50.png" data-base-u=
rl=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"im=
age/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-resour=
ce-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></=
p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"26" src=3D"c37504c083bd72de4bdd76ecf1f2fe3afbb4d506645f1510963422d6026=
98c22" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-10-5_9-4=
3-39.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664959419000&amp;api=3Dv2" dat=
a-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160796815" data=
-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" dat=
a-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-10-5_9-43-39.png" data-base-ur=
l=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"ima=
ge/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-resourc=
e-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></p=
>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p>In this example, the SCHEME_KEY is a HASH of SCHEME_INTERNAL_REF and SCH=
EME_LOB_GROUP.</p>
<p>For consistency, these should all be generated using the following funct=
ion:<br><strong>curated_idw.FNC_EDM_SKEY</strong></p>
<p>In the above, this will apply as follows:<br><br></p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluenc=
e-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" src=3D"43081f6255087d26e87fe5c2180d7b=
c6d74c710ab0da34fe1d06f72dfcf7ad46" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments=
/154629394/image2022-9-26_17-3-4.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D166=
4208184000&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-re=
source-id=3D"154629429" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-reso=
urce-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9-=
26_17-3-4.png" data-base-url=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-r=
esource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154=
629394" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D=
"" width=3D"468" height=3D"18"></span></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-DimensionTables">Dimension Ta=
bles</h1>
<p>Dimension tables are entities that add context to a dimensional model. T=
hey hold attributes that can be descriptive and give the Fact tables meanin=
g. Dimensions are sometimes referred to as Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCDs=
) which applies a methodology for tracking history over time.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"258" src=3D"44d5618f025651ab2935c15fe49e4f4a4ef5059ba8b5c06da4e20ca0de=
b2bcbc" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-9-26_16=
-26-49.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664206009000&amp;api=3Dv2" d=
ata-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"154629396" da=
ta-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" d=
ata-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9-26_16-26-49.png" data-base=
-url=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"=
image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span>=
</p>
<h6 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Figure1-SCDTypesasdefinedbyth=
eKimballGroup">Figure 1 - SCD Types as defined by the Kimball Group</h6>
<p>In our model, I have further categorised the dimensions as:</p>
<ul>
 <li><strong>Data Driven Dimensions - </strong>This is where source/silver =
layer data drives the population of the dimension</li>
 <li><strong>Reference Dimensions - </strong>This is where reference data d=
rives the population of the dimension</li>
</ul>
<p>These are categorised as such as they will be loaded in a different mann=
er and contain different default attributes.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>All dimension tables must also include an UNKNOWN or DEFAULT row that th=
e FACT table can join to when it fails to match the data. Control reporting=
 can be then be done across the model.</p>
<p>These will follow the same method in generating the keys.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Textual values will be UNKNOWN/UNK etc depending on the data being a des=
cription or a code.</p>
<p>Non textual values should have a default row of -1 e.g. curated_idw.FNC_=
EDM_SKEY(ARRAY('-1'))</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-DataDrivenDimensions">Data Dr=
iven Dimensions</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Attribute Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Column Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Domain&nbsp;</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Notes</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt; <strong>Key</strong></p>
     <p>E.g. Rating Quote Key<br><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt;<strong>_KEY</strong></p>
     <p>E.G. RATING_QUOTE_KEY</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Examples provided for&nbsp;</p>
     <p>Dimension Rating Quote / DIM_RATING_QUOTE</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be first column in the Dimension</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Effective Date Time</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_EFCTV_DTS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>*Dependent on SCD Type, not required on type 0,1</em></p>
     <p>Timestamp for row effectivity</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Expiration Date Time</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_EXPTN_DTS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>*Dependent on SCD Type, not required on type 0,1</em></p>
     <p>Timestamp for row expiration</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>The following should be the final 6 =
or 4* columns in a data driven dimension</strong></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Data Date Time</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_DATA_DTS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp that drives delta loads</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Create Date Time</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_CREATE_DTS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the row was written<=
/td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Update Date Time</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_UPDATE_DTS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the row was updated<=
/td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record Source Code</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_SRCE_CD</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Audit code to show which system the data originated</p>
     <p>For example, data populated into Gold, that originated from Silver =
CQS satellites: <strong>"CQS_EDW"</strong></p>
     <p>This will be managed via the notebook loads based on the dwh_contro=
l metadata (see Common Load Mechanism <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.n=
et/display/GIBP/Curated+BI+Data+Architecture" rel=3D"nofollow">Curated BI D=
ata Architecture - Data Platform - LV=3D Confluence - Production (group.net=
)</a>)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record Status Code</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_STATUS_CD</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Used in dimensions with high volume of source data wheen knowing th=
e status will be useful for performance, e.g. rating data.</p>
     <p><br>
       Partition column for entities loaded from rating to identify which r=
ating data is actually relevant to a policy</p>
     <p>EXP - Expired Rating<br>
       QTE - Quotes with no policy record (records will start here and then=
 move to EP or POL<br>
       POL - Policy system related, quotes of policies. Used to filter from=
 policy facts for performance purposes</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-ReferenceDimensions">Referenc=
e Dimensions</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Attribute Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Column Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Domain&nbsp;</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Notes</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt; <strong>Key</strong></p>
     <p>E.g. Date Key<br><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt;<strong>_KEY</strong></p>
     <p>E.G. DATE_KEY</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Examples provided for&nbsp;</p>
     <p>Dimension Date / DIM_DATE</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be first column in the Dimension</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>The following should b=
e the final 3 columns in a reference dimension</strong></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Create Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_CREATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was written</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Update Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_UPDATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was updated</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record So=
urce Code</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_SRCE_CD</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</t=
d>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Audit code to show which system the data originated</p>
     <p>Reference dimensions should be populated with "<strong>REF_IDW</str=
ong>"</p>
     <p>This will be managed via the notebook loads based on the dwh_contro=
l metadata (see Common Load Mechanism <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.n=
et/display/GIBP/Curated+BI+Data+Architecture" rel=3D"nofollow">Curated BI D=
ata Architecture - Data Platform - LV=3D Confluence - Production (group.net=
)</a>)</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-BridgeTables">Bridge Tables</=
h1>
<p>Bridge tables have multiple uses in dimensional modelling and are all to=
 do with relationships and granulairity.</p>
<p>They may sit between:</p>
<ol>
 <li>A Fact and a dimension=20
  <ol>
   <li>Traditionally each dimension will hold a single value at a consisten=
t level to a Fact tables defined grain.&nbsp; However, situations do arise =
whereby for the same period in time a dimension legitimately has multiple v=
alues. For example, a quote may decline for multiple reasons</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>Two dimensions=20
  <ol>
   <li>Two dimensions hold a many to many relationship, which we resolve wi=
th a bridge</li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-FacttoDimensionBridge">Fact t=
o Dimension Bridge</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Attribute Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Column Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Domain&nbsp;</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Notes</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Bridge Name Suffix&gt;&gt; <strong>Key</strong></p>
     <p>E.g. Rating Underwriting Result Key<br><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Bridge Name Suffix&gt;&gt;<strong>_KEY</strong></p>
     <p>E.G. RATING_UNDWG_RESULT_KEY</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Examples provided for&nbsp;</p>
     <p>Bridge Rating Underwriting Result / BRG_RATING_UNDWG_RESULT</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be first column in the Bridge</p>
     <p>Will hold the same key in the Fact</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt; <strong>Key</strong></p>
     <p>E.g. Underwriting Result Key</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt;<strong>_KEY</strong></p>
     <p>E.G. UNDWG_RESULT_KEY</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databr=
icks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Examples provided for&nbsp;</p>
     <p>Dimension Underwriting Result / DIM_UNDWG_RESULT</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be second column in the Bridge</p>
     <p>Foreign key to the dimension</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>The following should b=
e the final 4 columns in a fact to dimension bridge</strong></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Data Date=
 Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_DATA_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp that drives de=
lta loads</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Create Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_CREATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was written</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Update Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_UPDATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was updated</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record So=
urce Code</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_SRCE_CD</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</t=
d>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Audit code to show which system the data originated</p>
     <p>For example, data populated into Gold, that originated from Silver =
CQS satellites: <strong>"CQS_EDW"</strong></p>
     <p>This will be managed via the notebook loads based on the dwh_contro=
l metadata (see Common Load Mechanism <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.n=
et/display/GIBP/Curated+BI+Data+Architecture" rel=3D"nofollow">Curated BI D=
ata Architecture - Data Platform - LV=3D Confluence - Production (group.net=
)</a>)</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-DimensiontoDimensionBridge">D=
imension to Dimension Bridge</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
