td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>&lt;&lt;Dimension Name Suffix&gt;&gt;<strong>_KEY</strong></p>
     <p>E.G. INSURED_PERSON_KEY</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databr=
icks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Examples provided for&nbsp;</p>
     <p>Bridge Insured Object Persons / BRG_INSURED_OBJECT_PERSON</p>
     <p>to DIM_INSURED_PERSON</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be second column in the Bridge</p>
     <p>Foreign key to the second dimension in the bridge name</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>The following should b=
e the final 4 columns in a dimension to dimension bridge</strong></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Data Date=
 Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_DATA_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp that drives de=
lta loads&nbsp;</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Create Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_CREATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was written</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Update Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_UPDATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was updated</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record So=
urce Code</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_SRCE_CD</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</t=
d>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Audit code to show which system the data originated</p>
     <p>For example, data populated into Gold, that originated from Silver =
CQS satellites: <strong>"CQS_EDW"</strong></p>
     <p>This will be managed via the notebook loads based on the dwh_contro=
l metadata (see Common Load Mechanism <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.n=
et/display/GIBP/Curated+BI+Data+Architecture" rel=3D"nofollow">Curated BI D=
ata Architecture - Data Platform - LV=3D Confluence - Production (group.net=
)</a>)</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p>Attributes for context will normally be added to Dimension to Dimension =
Bridges, such as descriptions describing the relationship. In the example a=
bove, it maybe Role Description of the person against the object.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-FACTTables">FACT Tables</h1>
<p>A Fact table contains the key measures, ultimately defines the grain of =
the data that a user is looking at and will be the starting point of each q=
uery against the warehouse.</p>
<p>Defining the grain is possibly the most important part of the modelling =
process, once built, it can't change.</p>
<p>There are 3 types of Fact Table</p>
<ol>
 <li>Transaction - corresponds to a measurement take at a single instant</l=
i>
 <li>Periodic Snapshot - corresponds to a predefined time span</li>
 <li>Accumulating Snapshot - corresponds to a process that has a beginning =
and an end, as a process develops, the facts are often overwritten</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Attribute Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Column Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Domain&nbsp;</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Notes</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Fact Hash Key</p>
     <p><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>FCT_HASH_KEY</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">EDM Surrogate Hash Key (Databricks)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Should be a hash of all fields on the Fact table that make it uniqu=
e / define the grain.</p>
     <p>Won't be visible or used by end users when presented, but provides =
a more efficient delta join when loading.</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p>Should be first column in the Fact</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>The following should b=
e the final 4 columns in the Fact</strong></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Data Date=
 Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_DATA_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp that drives de=
lta loads</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Create Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_CREATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was written</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Update Da=
te Time</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_UPDATE_DTS</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Timestamp (Databricks)</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Audit timestamp of when the ro=
w was updated. The first 2 types should ever get updated, but this is inclu=
ded in case of data fixes.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Warehouse Audit Record So=
urce Code</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">DWH_REC_SRCE_CD</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Reference Code (Databricks)</t=
d>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Audit code to show which system the data originated</p>
     <p>For example, data populated into Gold, that originated from Silver =
CQS satellites: <strong>"CQS_EDW"</strong></p>
     <p>This will be managed via the notebook loads based on the dwh_contro=
l metadata (see Common Load Mechanism <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.n=
et/display/GIBP/Curated+BI+Data+Architecture" rel=3D"nofollow">Curated BI D=
ata Architecture - Data Platform - LV=3D Confluence - Production (group.net=
)</a>)</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Snowflaking">Snowflaking</h1>
<p>Snowflaking is a design process that is used to split dimensions into mu=
ltiple related dimensions. It could sometimes be considered a form of norma=
lisation, but can also be used to keep a model generic whereby multiple thi=
ngs may be on face value one type of data, but also be split into further m=
ore specific data.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Example:</p>
<p>In this example, property and caravan are both types of Insured Object.<=
/p>
<p>To avoid having an insured property key, insured caravan key and in time=
 an insured vehicle key in the fact, I have added a snowflake.</p>
<p>The snowflaked Insured Object holds the insured object type so that you =
know which key it corresponds to in the snowflaked dimensions, but if you a=
lready know from the Fact table and having joined to a product dimension, y=
ou could join directly to Dimension Insured Object Property using the Insur=
ed Object key from the fact, hence all relationships are shown on the model=
.</p>
<p>When we add in Dim Insured Object Vehicle, we don't need to do any addit=
ional work to the fact to add more foreign keys.</p>
<p>We could resolve this and generate some foreign keys logically for vehic=
le in views should we present a motor representation of this fact for examp=
le.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluenc=
e-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" src=3D"6f39d87efad83768f1b7b20ca26504=
657b94d49bc56bf691655376c5ce49dc49" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments=
/154629394/image2022-9-28_16-6-53.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D16=
64377613000&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-r=
esource-id=3D"160793442" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-res=
ource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9=
-28_16-6-53.png" data-base-url=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked=
-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1=
54629394" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=
=3D"" width=3D"468" height=3D"261"></span></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-AttributeNamingConvention">At=
tribute Naming Convention</h1>
<p>All attributes in the model across all entity types must have the follow=
ing applied</p>
<ol>
 <li>Class words</li>
 <li>The appropriate domains which normally mirror class words to set data =
types</li>
 <li>Meaningful Prefixes if relevant</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<p>In addition they must follow the following standards:</p>
<ul>
 <li>All attributes must adhere to the naming conventions as documented <a =
href=3D"https://confluence.group.net/display/GIBP/LV+Data+Naming+Standards"=
 rel=3D"nofollow">here in the LV Data Naming Standards</a></li>
 <li>Attributes in Dimension tables must conform to an agreed standard wher=
e appropriate and not be populated with multiple sources interpretation of =
similar data.&nbsp; If in doubt, a decision log should be raised for this, =
but conforming to the ABI lists has currently been agreed as a principle.</=
li>
 <li>The physical model should be run against the naming standards utility =
in ER Studio.=20
  <ul>
   <li>Choose Business Intelligence Naming Standards</li>
   <li>Source Logical, Target Physical</li>
   <li>Run translation</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-ClassWords">Class Words</h2>
<p>Class words should be added to every attribute to denote the type of dat=
a that is in the column.&nbsp; This should make it obvious to a user what t=
ype of data they are looking at just from the name.</p>
<p>They should be added as a suffix separated with an underscore, e.g. _AMT=
, _DESC, _CD</p>
<p>A definitive list is in 2.3.2.3 Class Word (required) <a href=3D"https:/=
/confluence.group.net/display/GIBP/LV+Data+Naming+Standards" rel=3D"nofollo=
w" style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">here in the LV Data Naming Standards</a=
></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Abbreviations">Abbreviations<=
/h2>
<p>Attribute names should follow the abbreviations list under A1 Standard A=
bbreviations and Acronyms List <a href=3D"https://confluence.group.net/disp=
lay/GIBP/LV+Data+Naming+Standards" rel=3D"nofollow">here in the LV Data Nam=
ing Standards</a></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Domains">Domains</h2>
<p>Domains are manged in ER studio and provide a way of providing consisten=
cy to data types. It also means that if we were to re platform, we could al=
ter the domains and all data types would change, enabling us to regenerate =
the model.</p>
<p>Domains follow the class words in what type of data it contains.</p>
<p>E.g.</p>
<p>An attribute with the Class word _CD will have the domain "Code (Databri=
cks)"</p>
<p>An attribute with the Class word _IND will have the domain "Indicator Al=
phanumeric (Databricks)"&nbsp; if the data will contain something like "Y/N=
/U" etc.</p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Prefixes">Prefixes</h2>
<p>Prefixes are optional ways to add more context to the attribute name if =
the attribute name is not descriptive enough as it is.&nbsp; A suitable des=
cription maybe the abbreviated source of the data.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Examplesfollowingthenamingcon=
ventions">Examples following the naming conventions</h2>
<p>Abbreviation Example:</p>
<p>In this example, the word construction has had a physical abbreviation a=
pplied, the word abbreviation ABI has been added to show that this field ha=
s been conformed to the ABI, and Description(DESC) has been added to show t=
hat it contains a descriptive text.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"123" src=3D"ebc3fafec8ea97f15126f211ba2590ce23cf0c42c8362b27a9ad20c1b7=
cb2fb1" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-9-28_12=
-33-57.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664364837000&amp;api=3Dv2" d=
ata-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160793016" da=
ta-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" d=
ata-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9-28_12-33-57.png" data-base=
-url=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"=
image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"209"></span>=
</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Prefix Example:</p>
<p>In this example, E4Q02 is data provided from the electoral role and mayb=
e known to some users, however to add context, a class word of Code(_CD) ha=
s been added, along with a prefix of Electoral Roll(ELTRL_ROLL) to indicate=
 the source of data.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"124" src=3D"a6d7ffaa7e0b6e7760475e8809ee21af52843fff01e73807ef0ca6eb7e=
3f8dfc" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-9-28_12=
-31-32.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664364692000&amp;api=3Dv2" d=
ata-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160793012" da=
ta-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" d=
ata-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9-28_12-31-32.png" data-base=
-url=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"=
image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"162"></span>=
</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Reference Domains:<br>
  In this example, it shows use of reference domains for Reference Dimensio=
ns.&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"130" src=3D"adc46605d77e963d45d76c944f5c7065be28208611ab686e8f6fc3ede4=
67321f" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/154629394/image2022-9-28_12=
-36-1.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1664364961000&amp;api=3Dv2" da=
ta-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"160793017" dat=
a-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" da=
ta-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-9-28_12-36-1.png" data-base-u=
rl=3D"https://confluence.group.net" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"im=
age/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"154629394" data-linked-resour=
ce-container-version=3D"27" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"218"></span></=
p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-InsertViews">Insert Views</h1=
>
<p>There should be an insert view per source to destination stored under <s=
trong>curated_idw_insert_views</strong></p>
<p>The naming convention is vw_ins_&lt;&lt;source system abbreviation&gt;&g=
t;_&lt;&lt;destination_entity_name&gt;&gt;</p>
<p>In the case of reference dimensions, these are static or sourced from re=
ference data and therefore will only have 1 per destination and therefore d=
o not require a source system abbreviation.</p>
<p>Examples:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Entity Type</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Insert view</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Destination Entity</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Ref Dimension</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">vw_ins_dim_transaction_type</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">dim_transaction_type</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Data Driven Dimension</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">vw_ins_cqs_dim_rating_quote</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">dim_rating_quote</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Data Driven Bridge</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">vw_ins_cqs_brg_rating_undwg_re=
sult</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">brg_rating_undwg_result</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Fact</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">vw_ins_cqs_fct_rating_insured_=
object_cover_options_trans</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">fct_rating_insured_object_cove=
r_options_trans</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"EDMEntityNaming,Definition&amp;Keys-Performance">Performance</h1>
<p>Performance tips for Dimensional Models on Delta Lake</p>
<ol>
 <li>Create a Z-Order on Fact Tables=20
  <ol>
   <li>Limit the number of columns to &lt;=3D4 and do this on the foreign k=
eys to the largest dimensions used by the Fact.&nbsp; If more than 4, prior=
itise the heaviest used</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>Create Z-Orders on Dimension Tables=20
  <ol>
   <li>Limit the number of columns &lt;=3D4 and focus on Z-Ordering the key=
 followed by those most likely to be included in a filter.</li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<p>Other considerations:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Analyze Table to gather statistics (ANALYZE TABLE &lt;&lt;DIMENSION&gt=
;&gt; COMPUTE STATISTICS FOR ALL COLUMNS</li>
 <li>Optimise file size for fast pruning. A good file size range is 32-128 =
MB</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
